    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "programmeDescription": "Criminology at Erasmus University Rotterdam studies how crime is defined, explained and addressed, and how it affects people and society. The programme combines criminological theory, social science, law and empirical research.",
    "comparisonExplanation": "Two UCR programs approach crime and justice through legal, social and behavioural inquiry, or through law and public authority. Both include actual criminal-law study, empirical methods and public-policy analysis. The first adds youth-radicalisation prevention and developmental and clinical perspectives; the second emphasises institutions, ethics and public intervention. Dedicated criminological theory, crime measurement, criminal careers, Dutch criminal procedure and the complete final research strand remain differences.",
